<title>USA: Fed's U.S. economic projections for 1997.</title>
<headline>Fed's U.S. economic projections for 1997.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are the economic projections of the Federal Reserve's Federal Open</p>
<p>Market Committee for 1997, compared to last year's actual</p>
<p>economic performance and administration projections.</p>
<p> (Q4 TO Q4)     ACTUAL     FOMC	    FOMC		ADMIN</p>
<p>		    1996	RANGE   CENTRAL TENDENCY</p>
<p> Nominal GDP    5.2    4.25 to 5.25  4.50 to 4.75	   4.6</p>
<p> Real GDP	 3.4    2.0  to 2.5   2.0  to 2.25	   2.0</p>
<p> CPI		3.2    2.75 to 3.50  2.75 to 3.0	    2.6</p>
<p> JOBLESS RATE*  5.4    5.25 to 5.5   5.25 to 5.5	    5.4</p>
<p>*Note: Actual and admin jobless is year avg, Fed jobless is Q4 avg.</p>
<p>In July last year the Fed forecast 1997 GDP growth of 1.75-2.25 pct, a CPI rise of 2.75-3.0 pct and a 5.5-5.75 pct jobless rate.</p>
</text>
